{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task AGENT-TF-01 is about implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. A call is accepted if:\n   - `parseable == true`\n   - `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return `accepted_call_ids` and `diagnostics` (in supplied call order)\n\nThe output schema requires:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted`, `call_id`, `normalized_gain`\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n- threshold: 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445, normalized = 1.18778445/5 = 0.23755689, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578, normalized = 1.26878578/5 = 0.25375716, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656, normalized = 1.03937656/5 = 0.20787531, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153, normalized = 1.18850153/3 = 0.39616718, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712, normalized = 1.30384712/6 = 0.21730785, parseable=true → accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.98682122 - 0.89260518 = 1.09421604, normalized = 1.09421604/4 = 0.27355401, parseable=false → NOT accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call4\"]\n\nThe candidate artifact mentions \"normalized_weights\" and \"stronger_counterfactual\" as hard contracts. Let me think about what these mean in Toolformer context.\n\nIn the original Toolformer paper, the filtering uses:\n- `L(i)` = cross-entropy loss over future tokens without the call\n- `L+(i)` = cross-entropy loss over future tokens with the call result\n- The gain is `L(i) - L+(i)`\n- Normalized gain is the average per-token gain\n\nThe \"stronger counterfactual\" might refer to using the minimum of the two losses without the call (or something similar). But looking at the fixture data, there's only `loss_without_call` and `loss_with_call`, so the computation seems straightforward.\n\n\"Normalized weights\" - in Toolformer, the loss is computed over prediction tokens, and the normalization is by the number of prediction tokens.\n\nLooking at the candidate artifact description more carefully:\n- \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" - this suggests we divide by max(1, prediction_tokens) to avoid division by zero\n- \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold\" - both conditions must be met\n- \"inclusive_threshold\" - means `\u003e=` not `\u003e`\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / max(1, prediction_tokens)\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 10),  # how many decimal places?\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the candidate artifact says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" What rounding? The schema just says `\"type\": \"number\"` - it doesn't specify precision. I'll just use the computed value without explicit rounding, or maybe round to a reasonable number of decimal places.\n\nActually, looking at the schema, `normalized_gain` is just a `number` type. I'll return the raw float value.\n\nLet me also think about validation. The candidate artifact says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\" So I should validate required fields.\n\nLet me also re-read \"Treat these registered properties as hard contracts: normalized_weights, stronger_counterfactual, inclusive_threshold, stable_order.\"\n\n- `normalized_weights`: normalize by prediction tokens\n- `stronger_counterfactual`: use the gain as the difference (the counterfactual being what happens without the call)\n- `inclusive_threshold`: use `\u003e=` for threshold comparison\n- `stable_order`: keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me finalize it.\n\nFor the rounding, the artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify decimal places. I'll use a reasonable precision like 8 decimal places or just return the float as-is. Actually, Python's default float precision should be fine.\n\nLet me write the final implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    \n    threshold = case.get(\"threshold\")\n    calls = case.get(\"calls\")\n    \n    if threshold is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: threshold\")\n    if calls is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: calls\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\n        for field in (\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"):\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Call {i} missing required field: {field}\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        tokens = max(1, prediction_tokens)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        \n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good. Now let me format it as the required JSON output with the `implementation` key.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: calls\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    required_call_fields = (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\\n        for field in required_call_fields:\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Call at index {i} missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        # Normalize by at least one token to avoid division by zero\\n        tokens = max(1, prediction_tokens)\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n\\n        # Inclusive threshold: accept iff parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        # Keep diagnostics in supplied call order (stable_order)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01jU4X6BuNWH3cFRi3eLAQIO","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2493},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2493,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":19,"output_tokens":2270,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1775},"service_tier":"standard"}}